te` fallback extends Node's narrower WHATWG decoder set with allowlisted `ISO-8859-16`/Latin-10 and DOS `CP437`/`CP775`/`CP850`/`CP852`/`CP858` IANA aliases without admitting transport codecs such as base64, hex, or UTF-7 as XML encodings. Supported multibyte encodings are decoded strictly: incomplete UTF-8, UTF-16, UTF-32, Shift_JIS, and other WHATWG sequences fail with `source_document_xml_encoding_invalid_bytes` instead of entering normalization as replacement characters. Data-URL charset metadata remains authoritative when an XML declaration is absent. Original-corpus API gates preserve representative Romanian, German, Baltic, Czech, Cyrillic, Japanese, simplified/traditional Chinese, Korean, and Euro labels through the complete release projection across memory, file, and SQLite alongside a big-endian UCS-2 Booklet, a little-endian UCS-4 Booklet, a UCS-4 IMS manifest inside ZIP, and malformed multibyte rejection\nrewrite-app/README.md:852:- Testtakers validation now follows the declared roster generation: monitor profile containers and references require schema 15.3, Booklet state presets plus extended monitor profile/filter fields require 15.4, and per-login `ViewSettings` require 17.6. Current 18.0 nested `ViewSettings` validate and preserve the original `theme`, `codeInput` type/length, and `monitorBookletVisibility` structure. Participant theme overrides and text, numeric, symbol, or alternative-symbol code entry now reach both the second-login-code and protected-block gates; keypad input uses the configured length and restores the application theme when the participant session ends. The byte-exact original 15.2 E2E roster imports and updates idempotently, while cross-generation feature mixing fails with stable diagnostics across memory, file, and SQLite\nrewrite-app/README.md:859:- loose source-package intake resolves unique original `Booklet` or `SysCheck` → `Unit` → Verona player, `DefinitionRef`, `VariablesRef`, coding-scheme, and separately uploaded `.i