pting routing syntax outside the XSD. In particular, `or` is accepted only on `Score`, as in the original schema; `Score` alone requires `of` plus `from`, while schema-valid missing references on `Value`, `Code`, and `Status` are preserved with the Original parser's empty-string/default-`0` representation instead of being dropped into an accidental fallback. Original unit resource IDs and ZIP-relative `CodingSchemeRef` files resolve into immutable releases, missing/malformed/newer-major schemes fail with stable import diagnostics, and the current Original's pinned `@iqb/responses@5.2.2` plus `@iqbspecs/coding-scheme@3.4.1` stack derives tracked codes, scores, indirect variables, and the exact IQB status rank server-side from raw IQB-standard Verona responses before selecting the first matching state option; only tracked base responses enter the coder, matching the Original's filtering boundary. Executable gates cover both textual `CODING_COMPLETE` and its numeric status comparison, plus the Original's comparable-value handling for null, booleans, sorted arrays, aggregate `NaN`/`Infinity`, and shallowly accepted malformed values without empty-string coercion across memory, file, and SQLite. The server persists the original-equivalent `BOOKLET_STATES` snapshot at launch and after response saves, restores or backfills it from durable storage, and uses it to remove inactive units from participant menus, sequential navigation, code-gate scans, timed-block expiry routing, and completion while rejecting direct hidden-unit jumps; Demo/Review/Trial now expose the original-style adaptive selector, persist its override separately from the automatic recommendation across saves and reloads in every storage backend, and immediately rebuild the participant route; run detail, open-run monitor cards, and CSV exports expose the effective state options to operators\nrewrite-app/README.md:872:- participant controller and Verona Player events now persist as first-class test-wide or unit