{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:31:51.050Z","ordinal":75378,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1078a-fa8a-7f61-a2dc-0a74a82de467","call_id":"call_7PseiBZQurzWc4TbgejAWkGP","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7fbced\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":873,\"output\":\"    { name: 'Mobile', width: 375, height: 667 },\\n  ];\\n\\n  for (const viewport of viewports) {\\n    console.log(\\n      `Testing ${viewport.name} (${viewport.width}x${viewport.height})`,\\n    );\\n\\n    await page.setViewportSize({\\n      width: viewport.width,\\n      height: viewport.height,\\n    });\\n\\n    await page.goto(TARGET_URL);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(1000);\\n\\n    await page.screenshot({\\n      path: `/tmp/${viewport.name.toLowerCase()}.png`,\\n      fullPage: true,\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  console.log('All viewports tested');\\n  await browser.close();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n## Available Helpers\\n\\nOptional utility functions in `lib/helpers.js`:\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst helpers = require('./lib/helpers');\\n\\n// Detect running dev servers (use this first)\\nconst servers = await helpers.detectDevServers();\\nconsole.log('Found servers:', servers);\\n\\n// Safe click with retry\\nawait helpers.safeClick(page, 'button.submit', { retries: 3 });\\n\\n// Safe type with clear\\nawait helpers.safeType(page, '#username', 'testuser');\\n\\n// Take timestamped screenshot\\nawait helpers.takeScreenshot(page, 'test-result');\\n\\n// Handle cookie banners\\nawait helpers.handleCookieBanner(page);\\n\\n// Extract table data\\nconst data = await helpers.extractTableData(page, 'table.results');\\n```\\n\\nSee `lib/helpers.js` for full list.\\n\\n## Custom HTTP Headers\\n\\nConfigure custom headers for all HTTP requests via environment variables. Useful for identifying automated traffic, getting LLM-optimized responses, or adding authentication tokens globally.\\n\\n**Single header (common case):**\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && \\\\\\n  PW_HEADER_NAME=X-Automated-By REDACTED \\\\\\n  node run.js /tmp/my-script.js\\n```\\n\\n**Multiple headers (JSON format):**\\n\\n```bash\\ncd $SKILL_DIR && \\\\\\n  PW_EXTRA_HEADERS='{\\\"X-Automated-By\\\":\\\"playwright-skill\\\",\\\"X-Debug\\\":\\\"true\\\"}' \\\\\\n  node run.js /tmp/my-script.js\\n```\\n\\nHeaders are automatically applied when using `helpers.createContext()`:\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst context = await helpers.createContext(browser);\\nconst page = await context.newPage();\\n// All requests from this page include your custom headers\\n```\\n\\nFor scripts using raw Playwright API, use the injected `getContextOptionsWithHeaders()`:\\n\\n```javascript\\nconst context = await browser.newContext(\\n  getContextOptionsWithHeaders({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } }),\\n);\\n```\\n\\n## Advanced Usage\\n\\nFor comprehensive Playwright API documentation, see [API_REFERENCE.md](API_REFERENCE.md):\\n\\n- Selectors & Locators best practices\\n- Network interception & API mocking\\n- Authentication & session management\\n- Visual regression testing\\n- Mobile device emulation\\n- Performance testing\\n- Debugging techniques\\n- CI/CD integration\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Each automation is custom-written for the specific request — not limited to pre-built scripts.\\n- Auto-detects running dev servers to eliminate hardcoded URLs.\\n- Test scripts written to `/tmp` for automatic cleanup (no project clutter).\\n- Code executes with proper module resolution via `run.js`.\\n- API_REFERENCE.md loaded only when advanced features are needed.\\n- Use `waitForURL`, `waitForSelector`, `waitForLoadState` instead of fixed timeouts.\\n- Always use try-catch for robust automation.\\n- **Playwright not installed?** Run `cd $SKILL_DIR && npm run setup`.\\n- **Module not found?** Ensure running from skill directory via `run.js` wrapper.\\n- **Browser doesn't open?** Check `headless: false` and ensure display is available.\\n- **Element not found?** Add wait: `await page.waitForSelector('.element', { timeout: 10000 })`.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"5a6bf5\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007916,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":585,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n/* Layout adapted from IQB Testcenter (MIT), aa627e196; see docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md. */\\n:host { display: block; min-width: 0; font-family: 'Nunito Sans', sans-serif; }\\n.login-page { display: flex; flex-direction: row; gap: 64px; height: 100%; color: var(--mat-sys-on-surface); }\\n.welcome-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; width: 25%; gap: 48px; max-height: 100%; overflow: auto; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 64px 24px 20px; background: var(--secondary-soft); }\\n.welcome-section img { width: 100%; }\\n.welcome-section .heading { font-size: 30px; }\\n.login-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: start; width: 75%; gap: 60px; }\\nform { margin-top: 64px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 80%; gap: 24px; }\\nh2 { margin: .83em 0; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 400; line-height: normal; letter-spacing: normal; }\\nlabel { font: inherit; color: inherit; }\\ninput.mat-mdc-input-element { font: inherit; border: 0; border-radius: 0; padding: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; }\\nmat-form-field { display: block; }\\n.login-submit { width: 15%; min-width: 120px; }\\n.login-submit:disabled { opacity: 1; }\\n.login-submit svg.mat-icon { width: 18px; height: 18px; }\\n.password-headline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; }\\n.password-headline > button { color: var(--secondary); border: 1px solid var(--secondary); border-radius: 12px; }\\nsvg.mat-icon { display: inline-block; width: 24px; height: 24px; fill: currentColor; vertical-align: middle; flex-shrink: 0; }\\n.password-field { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }\\n.password-field input { min-width: 0; flex: 1; }\\n.button-section { align-self: end; display: flex; gap: 9px; margin-top: auto; padding-bottom: 12px; margin-right: 24px; }\\n.button-section a { border: 1px solid var(--secondary); }\\n.login-problem { color: #a12020; }\\n.help-box { display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; justify-content: start;\\n  padding: 10px 10px 10px 24px; border: 1px solid var(--secondary); border-radius: 10px;\\n  width: 80%; box-sizing: content-box; --mat-card-elevated-container-color: var(--mat-sys-surface); }\\n.help-box svg.warning-icon { width: 5%; height: 100%; color: var(--secondary); flex-shrink: 0; }\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"282a74\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008166,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1120,\"output\":\"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\\n<section class=\\\"login-page\\\" id=\\\"originalParticipantLogin\\\">\\n  <aside class=\\\"welcome-section\\\">\\n    @if (settings.assetUrl('loginIllustration'); as illustration) {\\n      <img [src]=\\\"illustration\\\" alt=\\\"\\\" />\\n    }\\n    <div>\\n      <p class=\\\"heading\\\">{{ view.customText('login_sidepanel_title', 'Willkommen im IQB‑Testcenter') }}</p>\\n      <p>{{ view.customText('login_sidepanel_subtitle', 'Das IQB-Testcenter ist eine Anwendung des Instituts zur Qualitätsentwicklung im Bildungswesen (IQB) zur Durchführung digitaler Tests und Befragungen. Der Zugang ist mit den Zugangsdaten möglich, die Sie vorab erhalten haben.') }}</p>\\n    </div>\\n  </aside>\\n  <div class=\\\"login-section\\\">\\n    <form (ngSubmit)=\\\"submit()\\\" [attr.aria-busy]=\\\"busy()\\\">\\n      @if (!passwordStep()) {\\n        <h2>Anmeldenamen eingeben</h2>\\n        <mat-form-field appearance=\\\"outline\\\">\\n        <mat-label>Anmeldename</mat-label>\\n        <input matInput #nameInput id=\\\"originalLoginName\\\" name=\\\"name\\\" autocomplete=\\\"username\\\" autocapitalize=\\\"off\\\"\\n          [attr.aria-describedby]=\\\"problem() ? 'originalLoginProblem' : null\\\"\\n          required minlength=\\\"3\\\" [disabled]=\\\"busy()\\\" [(ngModel)]=\\\"view.runtime.loginKey\\\" />\\n        </mat-form-field>\\n      } @else {\\n        <div class=\\\"password-headline\\\">\\n          <button matIconButton type=\\\"button\\\" aria-label=\\\"Zurück zum Anmeldenamen\\\" [disabled]=\\\"busy()\\\" (click)=\\\"back()\\\">\\n            <svg class=\\\"mat-icon\\\" matButtonIcon aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 -960 960 960\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path d=\\\"M560-240 320-480l240-240 56 56-184 184 184 184-56 56Z\\\" /></svg>\\n          </button>\\n          <h2>Kennwort eingeben</h2>\\n        </div>\\n        <mat-form-field appearance=\\\"outline\\\">\\n          <mat-label>Kennwort</mat-label>\\n          <input matInput #passwordInput id=\\\"originalLoginPassword\\\" name=\\\"password\\\" autocomplete=\\\"current-password\\\"\\n            [attr.aria-describedby]=\\\"capsLock() ? 'originalLoginCapsLock' : problem() ? 'originalLoginProblem' : null\\\"\\n            (keyup)=\\\"passwordKeyUp($event)\\\"\\n            [type]=\\\"showPassword() ? 'text' : 'password'\\\" [disabled]=\\\"busy()\\\"\\n            [(ngModel)]=\\\"view.runtime.participantPassword\\\" />\\n          <button matIconButton matSuffix type=\\\"button\\\" [attr.aria-pressed]=\\\"showPassword()\\\"\\n            [attr.aria-label]=\\\"showPassword() ? 'Kennwort verbergen' : 'Kennwort anzeigen'\\\"\\n            (click)=\\\"showPassword.set(!showPassword())\\\">\\n            <svg class=\\\"mat-icon\\\" matButtonIcon aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 -960 960 960\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path d=\\\"M607.5-372.5Q660-425 660-500t-52.5-127.5Q555-680 480-680t-127.5 52.5Q300-575 300-500t52.5 127.5Q405-320 480-320t127.5-52.5Zm-204-51Q372-455 372-500t31.5-76.5Q435-608 480-608t76.5 31.5Q588-545 588-500t-31.5 76.5Q525-392 480-392t-76.5-31.5ZM214-281.5Q94-363 40-500q54-137 174-218.5T480-800q146 0 266 81.5T920-500q-54 137-174 218.5T480-200q-146 0-266-81.5ZM480-500Zm207.5 160.5Q782-399 832-500q-50-101-144.5-160.5T480-720q-113 0-207.5 59.5T128-500q50 101 144.5 160.5T480-280q113 0 207.5-59.5Z\\\" /></svg>\\n          </button>\\n        </mat-form-field>\\n      }\\n      @if (problem()) { <p id=\\\"originalLoginProblem\\\" class=\\\"login-problem\\\" role=\\\"alert\\\">{{ problem() }}</p> }\\n      @if (capsLock()) { <p id=\\\"originalLoginCapsLock\\\" role=\\\"status\\\">Feststelltaste ist aktiviert!</p> }\\n      <button matButton=\\\"filled\\\" class=\\\"login-submit\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\" [disabled]=\\\"busy() || !view.canSignIn || view.runtime.loginKey.trim().length < 3\\\">\\n        @if (!passwordStep() && !busy()) {\\n          <svg class=\\\"mat-icon\\\" matButtonIcon aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 -960 960 960\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path d=\\\"M504-480 320-664l56-56 240 240-240 240-56-56 184-184Z\\\" /></svg>\\n        }\\n        {{ busy() ? 'Bitte warten …' : passwordStep() ? 'Anmelden' : 'Weiter' }}\\n      </button>\\n    </form>\\n    @if (browserCompatibility.originalWarning; as warning) {\\n      <mat-card class=\\\"help-box\\\" role=\\\"status\\\">\\n        <svg class=\\\"mat-icon warning-icon\\\" aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 -960 960 960\\\" focusable=\\\"false\\\"><path d=\\\"m40-120 440-760 440 760H40Zm138-80h604L480-720 178-200Zm302-40q17 0 28.5-11.5T520-280q0-17-11.5-28.5T480-320q-17 0-28.5 11.5T440-280q0 17 11.5 28.5T480-240Zm-40-120h80v-200h-80v200Zm40-100Z\\\" /></svg>\\n        <mat-card-content>{{ warning.message }}</mat-card-content>\\n      </mat-card>\\n    }\\n    <div class=\\\"button-section\\\"><a matButton=\\\"tonal\\\" routerLink=\\\"/ops\\\">Adminbereich</a></div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0aeb0e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008458,\"e