{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:32:25.529Z","ordinal":76370,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a10768-b685-70b3-b721-445140bdea12","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6729a3d5-369d-45ee-ab00-453aaf2fab9b","process_id":"83146","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","npx ng build rewrite-app-web --configuration development --output-path /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development/dist/apps/web > /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development-build.log 2>&1 && UI_SMOKE_FRONTEND_ROOT=/tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development node scripts/smoke-deletion-confirmation.mjs > /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development-smoke.log 2>&1"],"cwd":"file:///Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"npx ng build rewrite-app-web --configuration development --output-path /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development/dist/apps/web > /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development-build.log 2>&1 && UI_SMOKE_FRONTEND_ROOT=/tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development node scripts/smoke-deletion-confirmation.mjs > /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development-smoke.log 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":43,"nanos":622741709},"formatted_output":"/Users/julian/.zprofile:source:8: no such file or directory: /Users/julian/.bashrc\n"},"started_at_ms":1791131501906,"completed_at_ms":1791131545529}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:32:47.054Z","ordinal":76371,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0a4b20de840ea00d016ac27f8fa0b487d2acb1c5df46d12feb","status":"completed","call_id":"call_vJdhA6lhP7u5Qol2Dwofqt2v","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\\n@@\\n - Required current-password confirmation for self-service password changes\\n   and for superadmin deletion of administrators/workspaces; resetting another\\n   administrator's password retains its distinct authorization boundary.\\n+  Administrator and workspace DELETE now require the acting administrator's\\n+  current password in `confirmationPassword`, after active-session and role /\\n+  delegation checks and before any deletion. Workspace deletion always requires\\n+  a platform administrator, even in diagnostic auth-off mode; its exact-key\\n+  confirmation remains required and the audit actor comes from that session.\\n+  The shared dialog keeps wrong-password errors inline, retains the selection\\n+  for correction, traps focus, prevents duplicate submissions while pending,\\n+  and clears its local secret on completion/cancellation/destruction. No secret\\n+  enters shell persistence or audit records. A failed directory read after an\\n+  acknowledged delete preserves the result instead of offering that deletion\\n+  again. Full Memory/file/SQLite suites pass 161 each; 144 core and 60 frontend\\n+  tests pass. Production/development builds remain within existing budgets.\\n+  Desktop/mobile gates exercise both interface preferences with the real API,\\n+  wrong-password retry, no-request cancellation, pending responses and failed\\n+  post-delete reads. The full protected SQLite operator sequence passes through\\n+  workspace and account batch deletion. This closes that functional deletion\\n+  gap, not pixel identity of the Original superadmin dialog or PostgreSQL proof.\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\\n@@\\n New administrator passwords use one deployment-wide policy in the API and Angular. `FIRST_SLICE_ADMIN_PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH` configures the minimum length from 1 through the fixed 60-character maximum (default `8`), while `FIRST_SLICE_ADMIN_PASSWORD_PATTERN` accepts a JavaScript regular expression (default `^.*$`). The policy applies to bootstrap, account creation, reset, mandatory change, voluntary change, and bulk-reset validation; existing credentials remain usable for sign-in and current-password confirmation after a stricter policy is deployed. Invalid settings stop startup and runtime preflight, and the effective secret-free policy is exposed through `/diagnostics/config` so clients can render the same feedback and native input constraints.\\n+\\n+Irreversible administrator and workspace deletion require the signed-in actor's\\n+current password, not the deleted user's password. Send `confirmationPassword`\\n+in the DELETE JSON body. Workspace deletion additionally requires its exact\\n+`confirmation` key and an active platform administrator, including when general\\n+diagnostic operator authentication is disabled. Missing confirmation returns\\n+`400 admin_password_confirmation_required`; incorrect or overlong confirmation\\n+returns `403 admin_password_confirmation_invalid` without deleting data. Existing\\n+role, delegation and self-deletion guards remain in force. The UI asks again in\\n+a local password dialog and keeps a wrong-password failure open for correction.\\n+Cancellation sends no DELETE, pending submission cannot be duplicated, and\\n+secrets never enter browser persistence or audit payloads. Directory-read failure\\n+after an acknowledged deletion is reported separately and does not erase the\\n+successful result. `npm run smoke:ui:deletion-confirmation:built` verifies these\\n+paths against an owned SQLite API at desktop/mobile sizes in both UI preferences.\\n*** Update File: /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\\n@@\\n ## Acceptance matrix\\n \\n+The Original 19.0 deletion password requirement is now enforced in shared\\n+administrator/workspace services and the UI. Both interface preferences use the\\n+same safe confirmation flow; desktop/mobile production/development tests cover\\n+wrong-password retry, focus, no-request cancellation, pending duplicate guards,\\n+and directory-read failure after a real acknowledged deletion. The password is\\n+dialog-local, never persisted. Its readable opaque surface is regression-tested.\\n+This is functional parity, not the Original Material superadmin dialog rendering;\\n+that page/dialog remains part of the open administration row below.\\n+\\n+The previous login publication's PostgreSQL UI job raced the Material saved-report\\n+dialog autofocus immediately after its animation. The full smoke now waits for\\n+the required in-dialog focus state itself before testing Tab/Shift+Tab; no focus\\n+assertion or timeout is removed. The protected SQLite full operator gate passes\\n+this save/focus sequence and continues through workspace/account deletion.\\n+Fresh complete PostgreSQL and publication CI proof remain separate requirements.\\n+\\n Latest login comparison: both name and password fixtures now match the actual\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -10 /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-production-smoke.log\\ntail -10 /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-development-smoke.log\\ncommand -v postgres pg_ctl psql\\nrg -n 'npm run ci:browser:ops|verify-ui-ops|verify-ops|deletion-confirmation' ../.github/workflows/rewrite-app-ci.yml\\nrg 'bundle initial|Output location' /tmp/testcenter-deletion-step-up-production-build.log\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app\",\"max_output_tokens\":1300}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10768-b685-70b3-b721-445140bdea12","create_time":1791131503.874272}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T16:32:47.072Z","ordinal":76372,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07cfb-af30-7a62-8a81-f821103d611a","turn_id":"01a10768-b685-70b3-b721-445140bdea12","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-a6ac9ac9-d56d-4093-8624-75bd038be249","changes":{"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -29,2 +29,18 @@\n \n+The Original 19.0 deletion password requirement is now enforced in shared\n+administrator/workspace services and the UI. Both interface preferences use the\n+same safe confirmation flow; desktop/mobile production/development tests cover\n+wrong-password retry, focus, no-request cancellation, pending duplicate guards,\n+and directory-read failure after a real acknowledged deletion. The password is\n+dialog-local, never persisted. Its readable opaque surface is regression-tested.\n+This is functional parity, not the Original Material superadmin dialog rendering;\n+that page/dialog remains part of the open administration row below.\n+\n+The previous login publication's PostgreSQL UI job raced the Material saved-report\n+dialog autofocus immediately after its animation. The full smoke now waits for\n+the required in-dialog focus state itself before testing Tab/Shift+Tab; no focus\n+assertion or timeout is removed. The protected SQLite full operator gate passes\n+this save/focus sequence and continues through workspace/account deletion.\n+Fresh complete PostgreSQL and publication CI proof remain separate requirements.\n+\n Latest login comparison: both name and password fixtures now match the actual\n","move_path":null},"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -178,2 +178,19 @@\n   administrator's password retains its distinct authorization boundary.\n+  Administrator and workspace DELETE now require the acting administrator's\n+  current password in `confirmationPassword`, after active-session and role /\n+  delegation checks and before any deletion. Workspace deletion always requires\n+  a platform administrator, even in diagnostic auth-off mode; its exact-key\n+  confirmation remains required and the audit actor comes from that session.\n+  The shared dialog keeps wrong-password errors inline, retains the selection\n+  for correction, traps focus, prevents duplicate submissions while pending,\n+  and clears its local secret on completion/cancellation/destruction. No secret\n+  enters shell persistence or audit records. A failed directory read after an\n+  acknowledged delete preserves the result instead of offering that deletion\n+  again. Full Memory/file/SQLite suites pass 161 each; 144 core and 60 frontend\n+  tests pass. Production/development builds remain within existing budgets.\n+  Desktop/mobile gates exercise both interface preferences with the real API,\n+  wrong-password retry, no-request cancellation, pending responses and failed\n+  post-delete reads. The full protected SQLite operator sequence passes through\n+  workspace and account batch deletion. This closes that functional deletion\n+  gap, not pixel identity of the Original superadmin dialog or PostgreSQL proof.\n - Optional installation-wide refusal of passwordless logins and rejection of\n","move_path":null},"/Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -414,2 +414,17 @@\n \n+Irreversible administrator and workspace deletion require the signed-in actor's\n+current password, not the deleted user's password. Send `confirmationPassword`\n+in the DELETE JSON body. Workspace deletion additionally requires its exact\n+`confirmation` key and an active platform administrator, including when general\n+diagnostic operator authentication is disabled. Missing confirmation returns\n+`400 admin_password_confirmation_required`; incorrect or overlong confirmation\n+returns `403 admin_password_confirmation_invalid` without deleting data. Existing\n+role, delegation and self-deletion guards remain in force. The UI asks again in\n+a local password dialog and keeps a wrong-password failure open for correction.\n+Cancellation sends no DELETE, pending submission cannot be duplicated, and\n+secrets never enter browser persistence or audit payloads. Directory-read failure\n+after an acknowledged deletion is reported separately and does not erase the\n+successful result. `npm run smoke:ui:deletion-confirmation:built` verifies these\n+paths against an owned SQLite API at desktop/mobile sizes in both UI preferences.\n+\n Optional browser-computed proof of work can protect the three Original Testcenter credential boundaries independently. Set `FIRST_SLICE_PROOF_OF_WORK_SCOPES` to a comma- or whitespace-separated subset of `admin`, `participant`, and `second_code`; production deployments should normally enable all three. The admin and participant scopes protect every non-empty login identity, including empty-password attempts and passwordless roster entries, so omitting a required password cannot bypass the work factor and cheaply fill a login failure sink. Any enabled scope requires a server-only `FIRST_SLICE_PROOF_OF_WORK_SECRET` of at least 32 characters. `FIRST_SLICE_PROOF_OF_WORK_MAX_NUMBER` controls the SHA-256 search range from 1 through 10,000,000 (default `1000000`), and `FIRST_SLICE_PROOF_OF_WORK_TTL_MS` controls challenge lifetime from 1,000 through 600,000 milliseconds (default `120000`). With no enabled scopes, the existing sign-in contracts remain compatible and no challenge is computed.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/PARITY.md\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/README.md\nM /Users/julian/code/testcenter-rewrite/rewrite-app/docs/ORIGINAL-UI-PARITY.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791131567070,"completed_at_ms":1791131567072}}
